<title>BRAZIL: Transbrasil 1996 net slightly higher.</title>
<headline>Transbrasil 1996 net slightly higher.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian carrier Transbrasil issued the following statement on its 1996 consolidated results.</p>
<p>		   1996			    1995</p>
<p>    shr	    15.34 reais		   15.17 reais</p>
<p>    net	    46.7 mln			46.2 mln</p>
<p>    net rvs	871.1 mln		     779.6 mln</p>
<p>NOTE: All data in Brazilian reais.  </p>
<p>Transbrasil said its market share dropped to 21 percent in 1996 from 28 percent due to a reduction in its fleet. Moreover, the firm plans to &quot;intensify efforts&quot; to increase its share to 35 percent by 2003, it said.</p>
<p>The company also plans to set new flights to the Portuguese cities of Lisbon and Porto as well as Munich and Moscow by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Also this year, Transbrasil plans to increase its cargo businesses by creating a new carrier AeroBrasil Servicos Aereos, it said.</p>
<p>In 1998, Transbrasil plans to offer flights to Asian countries, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5415))</p>
